1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:02,711
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:02,794 --> 00:00:04,796
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:09,050 --> 00:00:10,635
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,719 --> 00:00:12,762
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,846 --> 00:00:16,599
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,683 --> 00:00:18,852
[in English] Oh, I like your office.

7
00:00:18,935 --> 00:00:20,937
- [Dmitri, in English] <i>Very nice.</i>
- [Viktor, in English] <i>My little home.</i>

8
00:00:21,020 --> 00:00:23,481
[in English] Audrey,
what are you doing there?

9
00:00:23,565 --> 00:00:25,525
[Mongki] <i>We're sending</i>
<i>a few more girls this time.</i>

10
00:00:25,608 --> 00:00:27,694
I don't want to do this anymore.
I'm leaving the group.

11
00:00:27,777 --> 00:00:28,945
Are you out of your mind?

12
00:00:29,029 --> 00:00:30,905
[in English] Why do you have
a hole in your window?

13
00:00:30,989 --> 00:00:34,617
[man, in English] <i>The Sokolov brothers</i>
<i>who attended the summit are imposters.</i>

14
00:00:35,243 --> 00:00:37,203
[Samir, in English] <i>I knew it.</i>
<i>We have been compromised.</i>

15
00:00:38,121 --> 00:00:39,289
[grunts]

16
00:00:39,873 --> 00:00:41,499
[in English] Ambassador!

17
00:00:41,583 --> 00:00:42,667
[Paldo] Where's the gang hanging out?

18
00:00:42,751 --> 00:00:44,210
Call them. Drinks are on me!

19
00:00:44,294 --> 00:00:46,880
PREVIOUSLY

20
00:00:47,464 --> 00:00:48,757
[Paldo] <i>I've left the group.</i>

21
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:51,426
<i>I can't take what they're doing anymore.</i>

22
00:00:51,509 --> 00:00:52,594
[Samir, in English] <i>Check the perimeter.</i>

23
00:00:52,677 --> 00:00:54,137
[in English] <i>We have a breach.</i>

24
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:56,931
[in English] <i>I repeat, we have</i>
<i>a security breach! Check the perimeter!</i>

25
00:00:57,015 --> 00:00:59,184
[grunting and groaning]

26
00:00:59,267 --> 00:01:00,852
[grunting and groaning]

27
00:01:00,935 --> 00:01:02,645
[Viktor, in English]
<i>Did you catch the thief?</i>

28
00:01:02,729 --> 00:01:03,605
[Samir, in English] <i>No.</i>

29
00:01:03,688 --> 00:01:05,398
[in English] I can help you find this man.

30
00:01:05,482 --> 00:01:08,359
[Dmitri, in English] <i>I know</i>
<i>a very good tracker, a man hunter.</i>

31
00:01:09,069 --> 00:01:11,654
I hope you got what you needed to take.

32
00:01:14,115 --> 00:01:16,117
[Paldo] <i>Someone's going</i>
<i>to kill me, Emerson!</i>

33
00:01:16,201 --> 00:01:17,410
- Do you understand?!
- Who?

34
00:01:17,494 --> 00:01:18,828
There! Them!

35
00:01:18,912 --> 00:01:20,580
[Emerson] <i>I'll take care of it.</i>
<i>I'll save you.</i>

36
00:01:20,663 --> 00:01:22,665
<i>Buckle up! Buckle up and duck!</i>

37
00:01:22,749 --> 00:01:25,001
- <i>Duck!</i>
- [multiple gunfire]

38
00:01:25,084 --> 00:01:27,170
[Dmitri] <i>Maybe Atoy can help us.</i>

39
00:01:27,253 --> 00:01:28,421
[in English] <i>Since he's a tracker.</i>

40
00:01:28,505 --> 00:01:29,839
[Audrey, in English] <i>I don't think so.</i>

41
00:01:29,923 --> 00:01:32,383
[music fades]

42
00:01:32,467 --> 00:01:33,468
[Emerson laughs]

43
00:01:33,551 --> 00:01:36,095
How's that, Paldo, huh?

44
00:01:36,805 --> 00:01:38,181
You owe me one.

45
00:01:38,264 --> 00:01:41,267
I want unlimited pares for life.

46
00:01:41,810 --> 00:01:43,353
[foreboding music playing]

47
00:01:43,436 --> 00:01:46,481
Emerson, think about the pares later.

48
00:01:46,564 --> 00:01:49,109
[Paldo] They're right behind us! Hurry up!

49
00:01:49,192 --> 00:01:51,486
- [energetic rock music playing]
- [gunshot]

50
00:01:51,569 --> 00:01:53,404
- [Paldo] Faster!
- [Emerson gasps]

51
00:01:54,739 --> 00:01:58,451
Wait. What's that? An atomic bomb?

52
00:02:00,745 --> 00:02:03,081
That's not an atomic bomb.
That's a bazooka!

53
00:02:03,164 --> 00:02:04,582
Move, or we'll be gone in a flash!

54
00:02:06,209 --> 00:02:07,293
[grunts]

55
00:02:09,629 --> 00:02:11,047
[grunts]

56
00:02:11,131 --> 00:02:12,966
[tires screeching]

57
00:02:13,049 --> 00:02:15,343
It's Atoy. Wait, he's calling. Hold on.

58
00:02:19,264 --> 00:02:21,015
Doesn't Atoy have a gun here, Emerson?

59
00:02:21,099 --> 00:02:23,059
Wait, wait, wait.
I'll ask, I'll ask. Be quiet!

60
00:02:27,814 --> 00:02:28,648
[music fades]

61
00:02:28,731 --> 00:02:30,316
[Emerson] Atoy, Atoy.

62
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:31,609
- [Atoy] Emerson!
- [Emerson] <i>Help us.</i>

63
00:02:31,693 --> 00:02:32,610
[Atoy] Emerson, where are you?

64
00:02:32,694 --> 00:02:34,279
We're near the extension of…

65
00:02:34,362 --> 00:02:36,364
Wait, don't be noisy!
No, we're at the extension

66
00:02:36,447 --> 00:02:37,490
- near Sampaguita! Huh?
- [Paldo] Hold on to this!

67
00:02:37,574 --> 00:02:39,409
Oh, okay, okay, okay! I'll come to you!

68
00:02:39,492 --> 00:02:41,077
- Hurry!
- Wait, I can't--

69
00:02:43,371 --> 00:02:44,998
- [tense music playing]
- I don't know how to--

70
00:02:45,081 --> 00:02:46,332
Atoy-- Go ahead.

71
00:02:46,416 --> 00:02:47,458
[gun clicks]

72
00:02:47,542 --> 00:02:48,918
[music swells]

73
00:02:49,002 --> 00:02:50,003
It's just like this.

74
00:02:50,086 --> 00:02:52,046
I don't know how to use this, wait!

75
00:02:52,130 --> 00:02:53,381
You can do it!

76
00:02:56,843 --> 00:03:01,097
[action music playing]

77
00:03:09,439 --> 00:03:11,149
[tires screeching]

78
00:03:11,983 --> 00:03:13,902
- [grunts]
- [tires screeching]

79
00:03:19,657 --> 00:03:20,825
[Paldo] Stop.

80
00:03:21,492 --> 00:03:22,535
[grunts]

81
00:03:26,581 --> 00:03:27,790
[tires screeching]

82
00:03:28,833 --> 00:03:29,667
‪[Emerson sighs]

83
00:03:35,506 --> 00:03:36,716
‪[Emerson breathing heavily]

84
00:03:38,676 --> 00:03:41,346
[breathing heavily]

85
00:03:41,429 --> 00:03:43,056
I don't want to. I don't want to.

86
00:03:43,139 --> 00:03:45,141
- I don't want to.
- Are you okay?

87
00:03:45,225 --> 00:03:47,227
No! I don't want to.

88
00:03:47,310 --> 00:03:49,938
I don't want to. I don't want to.
I don't--

89
00:03:50,021 --> 00:03:52,357
[breathing heavily]

90
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:57,320
[pensive music playing]

91
00:03:58,446 --> 00:04:01,199
Cita] Delfin said
when you were still a kid…

92
00:04:01,950 --> 00:04:03,076
[sighs]

93
00:04:03,159 --> 00:04:04,869
…you were a good kid,

94
00:04:05,787 --> 00:04:10,208
and he was sure you'd grow up
to be a good person.

95
00:04:15,713 --> 00:04:16,756
Really?

96
00:04:16,839 --> 00:04:19,425
Mmm, it's just that
you often hung out with the friends,

97
00:04:20,301 --> 00:04:23,721
but… you've changed too, right?

98
00:04:24,264 --> 00:04:27,058
And if Delfin were alive today,

99
00:04:27,141 --> 00:04:29,394
I'm sure he'd be proud of you.

100
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:32,146
[Emerson breathing heavily]

101
00:04:32,230 --> 00:04:33,481
[Emerson grunts]

102
00:04:33,564 --> 00:04:35,858
[Emerson] Start up!

103
00:04:35,942 --> 00:04:38,236
Start up. I'm not ready to die yet!

104
00:04:38,319 --> 00:04:41,155
[moaning]

105
00:04:42,824 --> 00:04:44,367
[Emerson grunts]

106
00:04:45,034 --> 00:04:47,287
Emerson, they're almost here.

107
00:04:47,370 --> 00:04:48,162
‪[panting]

108
00:04:48,246 --> 00:04:49,831
‪You must leave now.

109
00:04:49,914 --> 00:04:51,082
- Huh?
- I'll cover you.

110
00:04:51,165 --> 00:04:53,126
No, no! We're not leaving here--

111
00:04:53,793 --> 00:04:55,878
We're not leaving here. I'll help you!

112
00:04:55,962 --> 00:04:57,797
We'll both get out of here alive!

113
00:04:57,880 --> 00:05:00,383
- [somber music playing]
- [heavy breathing]

114
00:05:00,466 --> 00:05:02,302
- [grunting]
- [engine cranking]

115
00:05:02,385 --> 00:05:04,262
[panting]

116
00:05:05,179 --> 00:05:06,764
- Let's go.
- There they are. Come on.

117
00:05:06,848 --> 00:05:07,724
Let's go.

118
00:05:07,807 --> 00:05:10,768
- [action music playing]
- [gasps]

119
00:05:10,852 --> 00:05:12,228
[tires screeching]

120
00:05:12,312 --> 00:05:14,272
[Emerson] What did you do to Mongki?
Why won't he stop hounding you?!

121
00:05:24,991 --> 00:05:27,952
[action music playing]

122
00:05:31,831 --> 00:05:32,665
‪[gasping]

123
00:05:36,919 --> 00:05:38,921
My God! They're here!

124
00:05:39,005 --> 00:05:40,590
Lord, take them already, please!

125
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:43,801
[Paldo] Emerson!

126
00:05:43,885 --> 00:05:45,553
- Just leave me!
- No, no!

127
00:05:45,636 --> 00:05:47,388
[Emerson] We're both getting out of here!

128
00:05:49,432 --> 00:05:50,266
‪[Emerson grunts]

129
00:05:51,100 --> 00:05:52,477
Emerson, you need
to make sure you survive!

130
00:05:52,560 --> 00:05:54,187
You need to tell Atoy the truth!

131
00:05:55,521 --> 00:05:56,481
What truth?!

132
00:06:00,568 --> 00:06:01,861
[groans]

133
00:06:02,445 --> 00:06:03,613
- [Paldo grunts]
- Paldo!

134
00:06:05,907 --> 00:06:07,116
[Emerson] Paldo.

135
00:06:10,161 --> 00:06:12,455
[energetic rock music playing]

136
00:06:12,830 --> 00:06:13,664
‪Move.

137
00:06:14,707 --> 00:06:16,292
[man] Move!

138
00:06:18,544 --> 00:06:19,378
‪[grunts]

139
00:06:20,713 --> 00:06:21,547
‪Paldo..

140
00:06:23,007 --> 00:06:24,092
[Emerson] Paldo.

141
00:06:25,384 --> 00:06:27,261
[grunts] Son of a thread!
What happened to you guys?

142
00:06:27,345 --> 00:06:28,971
Atoy, I missed you.

143
00:06:29,055 --> 00:06:30,264
This, this is what happened!

144
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:34,060
[in English] Cover. Cover fire.

145
00:06:34,143 --> 00:06:36,479
- What? What is that?
- Shoot them!

146
00:06:36,562 --> 00:06:38,022
[Emerson gasping]

147
00:06:39,232 --> 00:06:41,776
- [Emerson grunts]
- [Atoy mutters]

148
00:06:45,530 --> 00:06:46,364
‪[grunts, panting]

149
00:06:46,948 --> 00:06:48,074
[groans]

150
00:06:48,157 --> 00:06:50,451
What did you do to Mongki?
Why is he chasing you, huh?

151
00:06:51,160 --> 00:06:52,120
- [Paldo] Atoy, you should leave now!
- [Emerson grunts]

152
00:06:52,203 --> 00:06:53,496
Leave me. Go on!

153
00:06:53,579 --> 00:06:55,748
[Atoy] Hey! What the hell?!
Are you going crazy?

154
00:06:55,832 --> 00:06:57,708
- [Paldo groans]
- [Atoy] Paldo!

155
00:06:57,792 --> 00:06:58,751
What is your problem!?

156
00:06:58,835 --> 00:07:00,002
What's happening to you?

157
00:07:01,045 --> 00:07:02,880
- You need to know something.
- [Emerson gasps]

158
00:07:02,964 --> 00:07:04,507
[Emerson panting] Atoy, they're here!

159
00:07:06,592 --> 00:07:08,344
- It's about your father.
- [Emerson gasps]

160
00:07:08,427 --> 00:07:09,887
- [music fades]
- [heavy breathing]

161
00:07:10,721 --> 00:07:14,058
[sauve theme music playing]

162
00:07:37,582 --> 00:07:38,708
What about my father?

163
00:07:38,791 --> 00:07:40,793
- [sighs]
- [Atoy] Paldo.

164
00:07:40,877 --> 00:07:42,795
I was inside the vehicle.

165
00:07:43,838 --> 00:07:44,714
But I couldn't do anything.

166
00:07:44,797 --> 00:07:47,425
[sobs] Nothing, I couldn't do anything.

167
00:07:47,508 --> 00:07:49,343
[sobbing] I couldn't do anything.

168
00:07:49,427 --> 00:07:51,012
I couldn't save your dad.

169
00:07:51,095 --> 00:07:52,555
[heavy breathing]

170
00:07:52,638 --> 00:07:54,599
- [somber music playing]
- Atoy, forgive me.

171
00:07:54,682 --> 00:07:56,100
What are you saying?

172
00:07:58,769 --> 00:07:59,896
[car revving, tires screeching]

173
00:07:59,979 --> 00:08:01,522
[crashes]

174
00:08:05,276 --> 00:08:06,861
[groans]

175
00:08:07,487 --> 00:08:08,529
[epic music playing]

176
00:08:08,613 --> 00:08:10,198
What are you saying?!

177
00:08:11,532 --> 00:08:13,784
The day your dad got hit-and-run…

178
00:08:15,912 --> 00:08:17,455
you were really his target

179
00:08:17,538 --> 00:08:19,874
because you compromised
the shipment at the port.

180
00:08:20,666 --> 00:08:21,834
But I didn't-- [sobs]

181
00:08:21,918 --> 00:08:23,878
I couldn't do anything to stop it.

182
00:08:23,961 --> 00:08:27,590
[sobbing]

183
00:08:30,676 --> 00:08:31,636
[sighs]

184
00:08:33,095 --> 00:08:35,223
You ran over my dad?

185
00:08:38,559 --> 00:08:39,560
It wasn't me.

186
00:08:41,062 --> 00:08:42,271
- Who did it?
- [heavy breathing]

187
00:08:43,606 --> 00:08:45,399
- Not me.
- [Atoy] Who?

188
00:08:46,275 --> 00:08:47,235
Red.

189
00:08:47,318 --> 00:08:48,861
[music fades]

190
00:08:48,945 --> 00:08:51,572
Red Regalia was the one who hit your dad.

191
00:08:52,365 --> 00:08:53,491
[dramatic music playing]

192
00:08:53,574 --> 00:08:57,828
He… He's the one
who killed your dad, not me, Atoy!

193
00:08:59,330 --> 00:09:01,958
[Paldo groans, heavy breathing]

194
00:09:04,168 --> 00:09:05,878
I'm almost out of bullets, Atoy.

195
00:09:07,296 --> 00:09:08,130
‪[gasps]

196
00:09:08,548 --> 00:09:10,466
Here, eat this! [grunts]

197
00:09:10,550 --> 00:09:13,761
- [ominous music playing]
- [Atoy grunts]

198
00:09:14,512 --> 00:09:15,346
[shouts]

199
00:09:16,806 --> 00:09:18,849
‪[grunts]

200
00:09:18,933 --> 00:09:21,519
Atoy, you should leave now.
I'll handle this!

201
00:09:21,602 --> 00:09:23,646
- Go on!
- [Mongki] Let's go, let's go!

202
00:09:24,272 --> 00:09:25,106
‪[guns cocking]

203
00:09:26,816 --> 00:09:27,900
I'm not done with you yet.

204
00:09:28,818 --> 00:09:30,987
'Son, let's go!
Let's go, let's go, let's go!

205
00:09:31,571 --> 00:09:33,155
This will be my karma if I die.

206
00:09:34,031 --> 00:09:35,992
- Come on!
- [Paldo] Go on, get out of here!

207
00:09:36,075 --> 00:09:37,410
Emerson, go now!

208
00:09:38,744 --> 00:09:39,996
Paldo.

209
00:09:50,339 --> 00:09:52,049
[music fades]

210
00:09:53,551 --> 00:09:55,636
- [man] <i>I'll do that.</i>
- I'll take care of it, sis.

211
00:09:55,720 --> 00:09:56,762
- [Denden] You stay there.
- [Mona] That's enough.

212
00:09:56,846 --> 00:09:58,097
[Denden] So, we can still be quick.

213
00:09:58,180 --> 00:10:00,600
Oh, Karla! Hey, come with us!

214
00:10:00,683 --> 00:10:02,268
- We're going to hang out with the gays!
- [giggling]

215
00:10:02,351 --> 00:10:03,436
[girls, in English] Oh my God!

216
00:10:03,519 --> 00:10:04,562
- [Denden, in English] My God!
- [Jona] But wait, Denden.

217
00:10:04,645 --> 00:10:06,355
Karla doesn't go to bars.

218
00:10:06,439 --> 00:10:08,232
If it were basketball, however,
that's a definite yes.

219
00:10:08,316 --> 00:10:09,483
Oh, right. Yes.

220
00:10:09,567 --> 00:10:11,736
Um, okay.

221
00:10:11,819 --> 00:10:13,404
- I'm coming.
- [Jona] Oh!

222
00:10:13,487 --> 00:10:15,114
- [sneaky music playing]
- I don't want to go home yet.

223
00:10:15,823 --> 00:10:17,658
You can definitely join, of course.

224
00:10:17,742 --> 00:10:19,118
But that's a bar.

225
00:10:19,201 --> 00:10:21,871
[Mona] There will be drinking, tugs-tugs!

226
00:10:21,954 --> 00:10:23,914
- And cute boys, of course!
- [giggling]

227
00:10:23,998 --> 00:10:25,166
That's what matters!

228
00:10:25,249 --> 00:10:27,752
But do you have an outfit?

229
00:10:27,835 --> 00:10:28,669
‪[quirky sting]

230
00:10:29,378 --> 00:10:31,380
- Just this.
- That's it?

231
00:10:32,131 --> 00:10:34,967
Oh my, Karla, it's giving
water vendor on the corner vibes.

232
00:10:35,051 --> 00:10:36,552
It can't be like that!

233
00:10:36,636 --> 00:10:38,054
[Mona] That's why.

234
00:10:38,137 --> 00:10:39,347
I have a lot of clothes.

235
00:10:40,014 --> 00:10:42,350
Come with us,
then we'll give you a makeover!

236
00:10:42,433 --> 00:10:43,851
[Mona] Oh, there,
Denden will take care of you.

237
00:10:43,934 --> 00:10:44,977
- [Mona] What?
- [Denden] I got you.

238
00:10:45,061 --> 00:10:45,936
- Let's just help her out.
- Okay, okay.

239
00:10:46,020 --> 00:10:46,896
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

240
00:10:46,979 --> 00:10:48,105
- Let's go?
- Uncle.

241
00:10:48,189 --> 00:10:49,815
- We'll go ahead.
- [Kurt] Huh? Oh, okay, okay.

242
00:10:49,899 --> 00:10:51,067
- [Mona, in English] Bye!
- Take care, okay?

243
00:10:51,150 --> 00:10:52,652
- [Mona, in English] Bye!
- [Jona] They'll take care of you.

244
00:10:52,735 --> 00:10:53,903
- [Mona] Mmm-mmm.
- Let's go!

245
00:10:53,986 --> 00:10:55,488
[Denden] Let's help-- Let's help now.

246
00:10:55,571 --> 00:10:57,907
‪-[heavy breathing]
‪-[dramatic sting]

247
00:10:59,033 --> 00:11:01,452
[rousing music playing]

248
00:11:12,713 --> 00:11:14,799
[police siren wailing]

249
00:11:16,133 --> 00:11:18,135
Let's go. Let's go, go, go!

250
00:11:22,848 --> 00:11:24,850
[music swells]

251
00:11:28,104 --> 00:11:28,938
‪[dramatic sting]

252
00:11:35,653 --> 00:11:37,905
Red Regalia was the one
who ran over your dad!

253
00:11:37,988 --> 00:11:38,823
‪[dramatic stinging]

254
00:11:46,914 --> 00:11:49,291
[Atoy] <i>This is what I'll do</i>
<i>to the person who ran over my dad.</i>

255
00:11:52,378 --> 00:11:54,338
[Mongki] Boss, Paldo escaped.

256
00:11:55,214 --> 00:11:56,257
Well, what's new with that?

257
00:11:56,340 --> 00:11:59,009
There were two men who helped him.

258
00:11:59,093 --> 00:12:01,387
But I saw the vehicle they used.

259
00:12:01,887 --> 00:12:03,639
I didn't see Atoy,

260
00:12:03,722 --> 00:12:05,766
but the vehicle they used belongs to Atoy!

261
00:12:06,642 --> 00:12:07,852
And you still didn't catch him?

262
00:12:07,935 --> 00:12:09,353
No, boss.

263
00:12:10,312 --> 00:12:12,148
But this has a connection to Atoy.

264
00:12:12,940 --> 00:12:14,817
Why don't we just go back for Atoy?

265
00:12:14,900 --> 00:12:17,862
I have a feeling
that Paldo is really a spy!

266
00:12:18,654 --> 00:12:20,156
[pensive music playing]

267
00:12:20,239 --> 00:12:21,282
No.

268
00:12:21,866 --> 00:12:24,201
We should've been caught by Atoy
if that were the case.

269
00:12:25,703 --> 00:12:27,872
Let's not touch him for now.
His time will come.

270
00:12:29,540 --> 00:12:30,666
Where does Paldo live?

271
00:12:30,749 --> 00:12:31,876
Let's pay him a visit.

272
00:12:32,626 --> 00:12:33,794
[music fades]

273
00:12:34,378 --> 00:12:37,256
[in English] <i>This is unacceptable!</i>

274
00:12:38,591 --> 00:12:40,551
[Viktor, in English] <i>Whoever attacked me</i>

275
00:12:41,218 --> 00:12:45,973
<i>and stole from my office</i>
<i>is an enemy of our country,</i>

276
00:12:46,056 --> 00:12:50,644
<i>and whoever is connected with him</i>

277
00:12:50,728 --> 00:12:53,981
<i>is also an enemy of our country.</i>

278
00:12:55,149 --> 00:12:57,109
[in English] <i>They will pay.</i>

279
00:12:58,319 --> 00:13:00,696
[in English] <i>We will find you.</i>

280
00:13:01,530 --> 00:13:03,282
[news reporter] <i>According to authorities,</i>

281
00:13:03,365 --> 00:13:05,409
<i>the suspect was able to enter and exit</i>

282
00:13:05,493 --> 00:13:09,330
<i>through a small hole</i>
<i>on the ninth floor of the building.</i>

283
00:13:09,413 --> 00:13:12,458
<i>The investigation continues</i>
<i>on how the suspect</i>

284
00:13:12,541 --> 00:13:15,461
<i>managed to get through</i>
<i>despite the tight security--</i>

285
00:13:15,544 --> 00:13:17,129
[in English] Oh my gosh, Dad.

286
00:13:17,838 --> 00:13:19,507
[in English] Good thing you're okay!

287
00:13:19,590 --> 00:13:21,258
That thief is evil!

288
00:13:22,426 --> 00:13:25,429
[scoffs] Wait, Martina.
We still don't know-- Uh--

289
00:13:25,513 --> 00:13:28,265
What if they're the bad ones?

290
00:13:28,349 --> 00:13:31,060
They're the ones who were robbed,
and yet they're the bad ones too?

291
00:13:31,769 --> 00:13:34,438
[in English] No, okay.
What I'm trying to say is…

292
00:13:34,522 --> 00:13:38,734
we don't know why they took
the laptop from the embassy office.

293
00:13:38,817 --> 00:13:42,238
Maybe there's evidence there
about his shady deals.

294
00:13:42,321 --> 00:13:44,156
[in English] I've heard rumors
about the ambassador.

295
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:47,409
[in English] That he supports genocide
in conflict countries.

296
00:13:48,953 --> 00:13:50,120
[in English] Come on, Audrey.

297
00:13:50,204 --> 00:13:52,581
[in English] Dad,
you should really rethink

298
00:13:52,665 --> 00:13:54,333
doing business with the ambassador.

299
00:13:54,959 --> 00:13:58,003
[in English] Audrey,
those are just rumors.

300
00:13:58,963 --> 00:14:00,589
[in English] I agree with Martina.

301
00:14:01,382 --> 00:14:04,593
The bad guy, the guy who stole,
he even hurt me.

302
00:14:04,677 --> 00:14:05,970
[sinister music playing]

303
00:14:06,053 --> 00:14:08,722
[in English] But that's only
because he was trying to escape.

304
00:14:08,806 --> 00:14:10,933
[in English] You weren't his target.

305
00:14:11,016 --> 00:14:12,851
He didn't hurt me, Dad.

306
00:14:13,435 --> 00:14:14,436
You know,

307
00:14:15,104 --> 00:14:18,107
it sounds like
you're the thief's accomplice.

308
00:14:19,316 --> 00:14:20,943
You're defending him so much.

309
00:14:22,069 --> 00:14:23,153
Are you two close?

310
00:14:25,239 --> 00:14:26,156
[in English] What?

311
00:14:26,866 --> 00:14:29,952
No! Ah-- How are we supposed to be close?

312
00:14:30,035 --> 00:14:31,453
I don't know him!

313
00:14:32,204 --> 00:14:33,831
[in English] It's a joke, Audrey.

314
00:14:34,582 --> 00:14:36,500
[in English] Stop being
so serious all the time.

315
00:14:37,001 --> 00:14:41,922
[rousing music playing]

316
00:14:46,719 --> 00:14:48,554
- [Emerson] 'Toy, 'Toy. W-wait, wait.
- [Ame] Hey!

317
00:14:48,637 --> 00:14:49,555
- [Atoy] Move, move!
- [Ame] What happened to you guys?

318
00:14:49,638 --> 00:14:50,973
What's your plan? [panting]

319
00:14:51,056 --> 00:14:52,558
I'm going to kill them.

320
00:14:52,641 --> 00:14:54,184
- Atoy. Wait, 'Toy.
- I'm going to kill that Red.

321
00:14:54,268 --> 00:14:56,604
Cal-- Calm down first, 'Toy.

322
00:14:56,687 --> 00:14:58,772
Your rage is clouding your decision!

323
00:14:58,856 --> 00:15:00,232
How am I supposed to calm down?!

324
00:15:00,858 --> 00:15:04,695
All this time, we've been interacting
with the people who killed my father!

325
00:15:04,778 --> 00:15:05,863
[Atoy] And Paldo?

326
00:15:06,530 --> 00:15:09,158
He knew all this time!
Why did he just tell me now?

327
00:15:10,200 --> 00:15:12,244
I understand. Okay, okay.
Let all your anger out.

328
00:15:12,328 --> 00:15:15,539
But remember, you are not a murderer.

329
00:15:16,457 --> 00:15:17,958
If you want to retaliate,

330
00:15:18,042 --> 00:15:20,336
do it it through legal means!
Isn't that what you taught me?

331
00:15:20,419 --> 00:15:23,130
- [in English] Legal?!
- Yes! Let's involve the police then!

332
00:15:23,213 --> 00:15:26,050
The police?! There is nothing
the police can do!

333
00:15:26,133 --> 00:15:28,677
They got away with it before, more so now.

334
00:15:28,761 --> 00:15:30,304
We don't have any evidence!

335
00:15:30,387 --> 00:15:32,097
And they're going to kill Paldo!

336
00:15:32,181 --> 00:15:33,599
[tense music playing]

337
00:15:33,682 --> 00:15:36,602
There is no legal way
for demons like that!

338
00:15:36,685 --> 00:15:38,228
- [Emerson] ‘Toy.
- [Ame] Hey!

339
00:15:38,312 --> 00:15:39,897
[intense music playing]

340
00:15:39,980 --> 00:15:41,607
Emerson, please stop Atoy!

341
00:15:41,690 --> 00:15:43,525
We don't know what he might do.

342
00:15:43,609 --> 00:15:44,777
How can I stop him?

343
00:15:44,860 --> 00:15:46,153
Do you want me to get killed by him too?

344
00:15:46,737 --> 00:15:49,531
[music swells]

345
00:15:52,368 --> 00:15:53,243
[man] Paldo?

346
00:15:54,244 --> 00:15:55,162
Paldo!

347
00:15:56,580 --> 00:15:58,999
Here. That's Captain's house over there.

348
00:15:59,875 --> 00:16:01,835
- [Red] Thank you.
- All right.

349
00:16:01,919 --> 00:16:05,172
[ominous music playing]

350
00:16:06,590 --> 00:16:08,592
Are you also looking for Paldo?

351
00:16:09,510 --> 00:16:11,470
I've been calling him,
but no one's answering.

352
00:16:15,057 --> 00:16:15,933
[guns cocking]

353
00:16:31,031 --> 00:16:35,411
[tense music playing]

354
00:16:39,415 --> 00:16:41,709
- [lively chattering]
- [elated shrieking]

355
00:16:42,418 --> 00:16:45,671
Here we are! Just in time!

356
00:16:45,754 --> 00:16:46,797
[exclaims]

357
00:16:46,880 --> 00:16:50,718
[in English] Barangay Tabang Lupa
beauties coming at ya!

358
00:16:50,801 --> 00:16:53,387
- [in English] Hello!
- [elated shrieking]

359
00:16:53,470 --> 00:16:55,723
- Hey, wait. Where's Karla?
- [Mona] Karla?

360
00:16:55,806 --> 00:16:57,349
- Yes.
- She was just here earlier.

361
00:16:58,809 --> 00:17:00,019
[Jona] Karla? Is that Karla?

362
00:17:01,437 --> 00:17:03,147
[Jona and Mona] Oh!

363
00:17:03,230 --> 00:17:04,398
[Mona] Karla.

364
00:17:04,481 --> 00:17:06,442
[Denden] Why the frown?

365
00:17:06,525 --> 00:17:08,027
Smile! Show off!

366
00:17:08,110 --> 00:17:09,778
[exclaiming]

367
00:17:09,862 --> 00:17:11,905
I'm just not used to this.

368
00:17:11,989 --> 00:17:13,198
I just wanted to drink.

369
00:17:13,282 --> 00:17:14,825
Karla, come on.

370
00:17:14,908 --> 00:17:16,452
You won't get in

371
00:17:16,535 --> 00:17:18,829
if you're wearing
basketball shorts and a T-shirt.

372
00:17:18,912 --> 00:17:20,831
- [Mona] Yes.
- So, it's fine, just go for it.

373
00:17:20,914 --> 00:17:21,790
[in English] Let's go!

374
00:17:21,874 --> 00:17:23,709
[lively chatter]

375
00:17:23,792 --> 00:17:25,919
- [Mona] Take it slow.
- We're gonna enjoy tonight.

376
00:17:26,003 --> 00:17:28,047
[lively chattering]

377
00:17:28,130 --> 00:17:29,465
[Denden] Just smile, smile!

378
00:17:32,176 --> 00:17:33,010
‪[Jona gasps]

379
00:17:33,886 --> 00:17:35,429
‪-[indistinct chattering]
‪-[inaudible]

380
00:17:35,512 --> 00:17:38,849
[Denden] Hey! I'm gonna eat-and-run.

381
00:17:41,435 --> 00:17:44,396
- [Jona] So, what now?
- [Mona] Go, order.

382
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:45,564
[Jona] Denden, treat us.

383
00:17:45,647 --> 00:17:47,566
Wow, that's six months to pay off, huh.

384
00:17:47,649 --> 00:17:48,609
- Pay for your drinks.
- Drinks!

385
00:17:48,692 --> 00:17:50,903
- [in English] Thank you, baby, okay.
- Oh, wow.

386
00:17:51,779 --> 00:17:52,780
[Denden] Your 'babies'
are all over the place, huh?

387
00:17:52,863 --> 00:17:54,948
[Jona] But to brother, that's a baby. Oh!

388
00:17:55,824 --> 00:17:57,618
- [Jona] Here it comes!
- [in English] Cheers!

389
00:17:57,701 --> 00:17:58,786
- [in English] Cheers!
- [shrieking]

390
00:17:58,869 --> 00:18:00,412
I'll have water first.

391
00:18:02,706 --> 00:18:04,458
[lively chattering]

392
00:18:04,541 --> 00:18:05,876
Let's order some pares.

393
00:18:05,959 --> 00:18:07,294
[Denden] Oh, okay.

394
00:18:08,170 --> 00:18:09,296
Ah, babe, let's just stay here.

395
00:18:10,714 --> 00:18:13,175
I'll just order drinks at the bar,
okay, because…

396
00:18:13,258 --> 00:18:15,219
there's no waiter. Have a seat.

397
00:18:15,302 --> 00:18:16,678
Okay, babe. Thanks!

398
00:18:16,762 --> 00:18:18,055
This is where we're sitting.

399
00:18:18,138 --> 00:18:19,473
[in English] Oh, wait.

400
00:18:20,432 --> 00:18:22,267
[in English] Is that Karla?

401
00:18:24,061 --> 00:18:25,938
- [magical twinkle]
- [romantic music playing]

402
00:18:26,605 --> 00:18:27,689
It is her.

403
00:18:28,482 --> 00:18:30,067
This is the first time
I'm seeing her like that.

404
00:18:31,443 --> 00:18:32,736
[in English] She's trying way too hard.

405
00:18:32,820 --> 00:18:34,154
Her overall look is so cheap.

406
00:18:34,238 --> 00:18:36,365
The outfit is kinda gross.

407
00:18:36,448 --> 00:18:39,785
[in English] I know, right?
Like, what on earth is she wearing?

408
00:18:40,702 --> 00:18:43,539
You know, Karla's actually nice.
Don't laugh at her.

409
00:18:44,456 --> 00:18:50,254
♪ <i>It's not that Im thinking bad thoughts</i> ♪

410
00:18:53,841 --> 00:18:55,008
[music fades]

411
00:18:55,092 --> 00:18:58,345
[Ibyang] If Sister Karla
isn't on the basketball court,

412
00:18:58,428 --> 00:19:02,141
then, where could she possibly be?

413
00:19:02,224 --> 00:19:03,976
I honestly don't know.

414
00:19:04,059 --> 00:19:07,104
Let's just go back to the tailoring shop.
Maybe Atoy is there.

415
00:19:07,187 --> 00:19:09,148
Let's ask for help to find her.

416
00:19:10,691 --> 00:19:12,276
[Cita] Oh, Ibyang, why?

417
00:19:14,069 --> 00:19:16,530
- Miss Cita, you go on ahead.
- [melancholic music playing]

418
00:19:17,322 --> 00:19:18,740
I'll just go home.

419
00:19:19,408 --> 00:19:23,078
Ibyang, are you still sulking? Jeez.

420
00:19:23,162 --> 00:19:25,873
Atoy always asks me about you.

421
00:19:25,956 --> 00:19:28,500
He's sad that you're ignoring him.

422
00:19:28,584 --> 00:19:31,503
He just doesn't admit it,
but he really loves you.

423
00:19:33,964 --> 00:19:35,549
That's not true.

424
00:19:36,592 --> 00:19:38,218
You're just saying that.

425
00:19:38,302 --> 00:19:40,512
Huh? It's true!

426
00:19:41,972 --> 00:19:43,974
[car revving]

427
00:19:44,057 --> 00:19:45,309
[shouts] Ibyang!

428
00:19:45,392 --> 00:19:47,603
[Cita] Help me! Help!

429
00:19:47,686 --> 00:19:49,229
Ibyang, Ibyang!

430
00:19:49,313 --> 00:19:50,689
Help!

431
00:19:50,772 --> 00:19:53,066
Ibyang! Ibyang--

432
00:19:53,150 --> 00:19:55,235
- Help, help.
- [tense music playing]

433
00:19:55,903 --> 00:19:57,529
[Cita] Let's carry her.

434
00:19:57,613 --> 00:19:58,614
Help.

435
00:20:02,784 --> 00:20:04,870
Karla, we're stepping out for a bit.

436
00:20:04,953 --> 00:20:05,787
- Mmm-hmm.
- Just stay here, okay?

437
00:20:05,871 --> 00:20:06,705
- We'll be back.
- Just stay there.

438
00:20:06,788 --> 00:20:07,789
- Oh, okay.
- [Mona] Promise, okay.

439
00:20:07,873 --> 00:20:08,999
[Denden] Don't move.

440
00:20:09,082 --> 00:20:10,167
- Yes. Okay.
- [Jona] Just dance.

441
00:20:10,250 --> 00:20:13,003
- [Denden] Don't leave.
- [Mona] We'll be back.

442
00:20:13,086 --> 00:20:14,922
[lively chattering]

443
00:20:15,005 --> 00:20:16,340
[Denden] Just smile, smile.

444
00:20:17,174 --> 00:20:22,512
[lively chattering]

445
00:20:24,014 --> 00:20:26,141
Karla, take it slow.

446
00:20:26,225 --> 00:20:28,769
Gavin, hello! You're here too?

447
00:20:28,852 --> 00:20:30,979
When did you learn to drink?

448
00:20:31,063 --> 00:20:32,272
This?

449
00:20:32,356 --> 00:20:33,774
This isn't alcohol. It's just a mocktail.

450
00:20:33,857 --> 00:20:35,776
I don't drink.

451
00:20:36,443 --> 00:20:37,653
And also, why are you dressed like that?

452
00:20:37,736 --> 00:20:39,196
Why are you hanging out here?

453
00:20:39,279 --> 00:20:43,075
You know, those sudden changes
indicate you have a problem.

454
00:20:43,158 --> 00:20:45,118
You can just tell me, you know.

455
00:20:45,202 --> 00:20:47,079
Well, you're always busy.

456
00:20:47,162 --> 00:20:50,374
And besides, my problem is really tough.
You wouldn't understand it.

457
00:20:50,457 --> 00:20:52,334
Because you're a rich kid.
You can't relate.

458
00:20:52,417 --> 00:20:53,335
[in English] Try me.

459
00:20:56,129 --> 00:20:58,298
[Cathy] Uh, Karla!

460
00:20:58,382 --> 00:20:59,675
[in English] Wait!

461
00:20:59,758 --> 00:21:02,344
[in English] You look so, uh, cute!

462
00:21:02,427 --> 00:21:03,387
[Cathy chuckles]

463
00:21:04,054 --> 00:21:05,639
[in English] Do you want
to join us at the table?

464
00:21:06,556 --> 00:21:08,934
You poor thing, sitting there all alone.

465
00:21:09,685 --> 00:21:12,396
No, it's okay. I'm with Sis Denden.

466
00:21:13,355 --> 00:21:15,732
- Who…?
- [Karla] Denden.

467
00:21:17,985 --> 00:21:19,278
- [pensive music playing]
- Where are they? [chuckles]

468
00:21:19,778 --> 00:21:21,530
[Cathy] Come on. Don't be shy.

469
00:21:21,613 --> 00:21:22,781
[in English] Come on.

470
00:21:24,199 --> 00:21:26,827
[in English] Come on!
Join our table. We're just there.

471
00:21:26,910 --> 00:21:28,245
Come on. Let's go.

472
00:21:28,954 --> 00:21:29,871
[in English] Let's go!

473
00:21:34,167 --> 00:21:35,335
We'll just stay here.

474
00:21:35,419 --> 00:21:36,295
Here, have a seat.

475
00:21:47,389 --> 00:21:48,598
Uh, waiter.

476
00:21:51,393 --> 00:21:55,689
[suspicious music playing]

477
00:21:57,232 --> 00:22:00,694
One Amaretto Sour for him.

478
00:22:04,156 --> 00:22:05,407
'Toy, ah-- What are you gonna do?

479
00:22:05,490 --> 00:22:07,075
Emerson, get out of my way.

480
00:22:07,159 --> 00:22:09,786
'Toy, hmm-- Let's just drink!
Let's just drink!

481
00:22:09,870 --> 00:22:10,746
- 'Toy, wait-- Ah--
- Emerson!

482
00:22:10,829 --> 00:22:11,955
Ame, Ame, help me out.

483
00:22:12,039 --> 00:22:13,290
- Stand here and block him!
- [Atoy] Ame.

484
00:22:13,373 --> 00:22:15,709
As if my blocking will do anything.

485
00:22:15,792 --> 00:22:17,044
He'll just step over me.

486
00:22:17,127 --> 00:22:19,087
'Toy, 'Toy, think
about what you'll do first.

487
00:22:19,171 --> 00:22:20,172
- [Ame] Atoy.
- [Emerson, in English] Please?

488
00:22:20,255 --> 00:22:22,132
Ah, bro, you want to drink now.
I'll buy some ice!

489
00:22:22,215 --> 00:22:23,550
- [Atoy] Move aside!
- [both] Atoy!

490
00:22:23,633 --> 00:22:25,010
[T-Bak] Brother Atoy! [sighs]

491
00:22:25,594 --> 00:22:28,263
There are men outside

492
00:22:28,346 --> 00:22:31,099
Paldo's house.
Then they shot at his house!

493
00:22:31,183 --> 00:22:33,935
- [Emerson] Huh?
- They are the same men who came before.

494
00:22:34,019 --> 00:22:35,604
They were looking for you too!

495
00:22:36,480 --> 00:22:38,315
Mongki and the others.

496
00:22:38,398 --> 00:22:39,733
Maybe Red is with them.

497
00:22:39,816 --> 00:22:40,984
They're gone! Those guys are gone!

498
00:22:41,068 --> 00:22:42,027
- Those guys are gone.
- Oh, yes!

499
00:22:42,110 --> 00:22:43,487
- Maybe?
- What the heck is that about?!

500
00:22:43,570 --> 00:22:44,863
- Move!
- [Emerson] 'Toy, 'Toy, 'Toy, 'Toy!

501
00:22:44,946 --> 00:22:46,573
- Think about this first, Atoy--
- [Munggo] Atoy, Atoy!

502
00:22:46,656 --> 00:22:47,699
It's Ibyang!

503
00:22:47,783 --> 00:22:49,076
[Munggo] She was taken to the hospital!

504
00:22:49,159 --> 00:22:51,536
- She almost got hit earlier!
- [Ame] Huh?

505
00:22:51,620 --> 00:22:57,250
[intense music playing]

506
00:23:00,253 --> 00:23:02,631
Karla, don't you drink?

507
00:23:02,714 --> 00:23:03,924
No, not really.

508
00:23:04,007 --> 00:23:05,509
[Cathy] Come on, just try it!

509
00:23:05,592 --> 00:23:07,761
[cool upbeat music playing]

510
00:23:07,844 --> 00:23:10,055
Babe, she doesn't want to.
Don't force her.

511
00:23:10,138 --> 00:23:11,556
[in English] Okay, fine.

512
00:23:13,475 --> 00:23:15,769
- Are you having fun at least?
- [in English] Yes.

513
00:23:16,686 --> 00:23:17,854
- [Cathy] Hmm? Really?
- Yes.

514
00:23:17,938 --> 00:23:19,481
Doesn't seem like it!

515
00:23:19,564 --> 00:23:20,816
[in English] Come on! Let's have fun!

516
00:23:20,899 --> 00:23:22,984
[in English] Gavin, come on.
Let's dance. Let's dance!

517
00:23:24,152 --> 00:23:26,154
[Cathy giggles]

518
00:23:26,863 --> 00:23:28,907
[in English] Come on! Karla!

519
00:23:28,990 --> 00:23:31,409
[in English] I dare you to…

520
00:23:31,493 --> 00:23:33,036
dance on top of the chair.

521
00:23:33,703 --> 00:23:35,497
- [in English] Babe.
- [Cathy, in English] Come on!

522
00:23:36,414 --> 00:23:40,502
Karla! Karla! Karla! Karla! Karla!

523
00:23:41,128 --> 00:23:42,170
[Cathy] Go ahead!

524
00:23:42,754 --> 00:23:44,297
[Cathy whoops and chuckles]

525
00:23:44,381 --> 00:23:46,049
- [Gavin] Karla, just take it slow, okay?
- [in English] Go!

526
00:23:46,133 --> 00:23:48,301
- [whoops]
- [Cathy, in English] More! Let's go.

527
00:23:48,385 --> 00:23:49,344
[in English] Dance-off!

528
00:23:49,427 --> 00:23:50,387
- [in English] Let's go!
- [in English] Yes!

529
00:23:50,470 --> 00:23:53,014
Go! Keep going! [whoops, chuckles]

530
00:23:53,098 --> 00:23:54,391
[Gavin] Karla, stop.

531
00:23:54,474 --> 00:23:56,977
- You might get hurt.
- [Karla] No, it's okay.

532
00:23:58,478 --> 00:24:00,272
- [Gavin] Karla, come down, come down.
- [Cathy, in English] Come on, Karla!

533
00:24:02,899 --> 00:24:05,485
[in English] Babe, stop doing this to her.
You're making fun of her.

534
00:24:06,361 --> 00:24:09,114
[in English] Gavin,
we're having fun with her!

535
00:24:13,785 --> 00:24:15,453
Karla, where are your friends anyway?

536
00:24:15,537 --> 00:24:16,872
Sis Denden and the others?

537
00:24:17,747 --> 00:24:19,124
They might have gone back already.

538
00:24:20,292 --> 00:24:21,710
Ah, I'll just go find them.

539
00:24:27,382 --> 00:24:30,343
[pensive music playing]

540
00:24:30,427 --> 00:24:31,511
[sighs]

541
00:24:33,555 --> 00:24:35,765
We saw you dancing earlier.

542
00:24:36,641 --> 00:24:38,268
- Let's dance there.
- Is that okay?

543
00:24:39,186 --> 00:24:40,395
Come join us.

544
00:24:40,478 --> 00:24:43,106
[suspicious music playing]

545
00:24:43,190 --> 00:24:46,234
[ambulance siren wailing]

546
00:25:03,376 --> 00:25:04,461
Uh…

547
00:25:06,004 --> 00:25:09,591
Miss Cita already talked to the doctor.

548
00:25:10,383 --> 00:25:13,511
[Emerson] They said
Ibyang's CT scan result is okay, so…

549
00:25:13,595 --> 00:25:15,263
she's ready for discharge.

550
00:25:15,972 --> 00:25:17,974
Miss Cita is at the cashier now.

551
00:25:22,187 --> 00:25:23,188
Thanks.

552
00:25:29,569 --> 00:25:32,822
[melancholic music playing]

553
00:25:34,407 --> 00:25:36,201
Where am I?

554
00:25:36,701 --> 00:25:37,786
Ibyang.

555
00:25:38,536 --> 00:25:39,537
Ibyang.

556
00:25:43,500 --> 00:25:44,584
[Atoy] You're at the hospital.

557
00:25:45,502 --> 00:25:46,336
‪[inhales]

558
00:25:47,128 --> 00:25:49,047
The vehicle sideswiped you.

559
00:25:49,881 --> 00:25:51,132
You got hit.

560
00:25:52,008 --> 00:25:54,135
You fell pretty hard.

561
00:25:57,097 --> 00:25:59,724
Do you remember
what kind of vehicle it was?

562
00:26:02,978 --> 00:26:04,312
Well…

563
00:26:04,896 --> 00:26:07,774
The vehicle was moving quickly.

564
00:26:08,608 --> 00:26:09,693
Exactly. [clicks tongue]

565
00:26:11,027 --> 00:26:12,570
My God, Ibyang.

566
00:26:13,238 --> 00:26:15,282
Next time, be careful, okay?

567
00:26:16,157 --> 00:26:18,034
Watch where you're going.

568
00:26:18,118 --> 00:26:19,953
When you step out
on the road, look around.

569
00:26:20,036 --> 00:26:23,248
All the passing vehicles,
any one of them can hit you.

570
00:26:23,331 --> 00:26:24,582
And you're still so little!

571
00:26:26,960 --> 00:26:29,087
Are you mad at me?

572
00:26:29,170 --> 00:26:30,255
No!

573
00:26:34,259 --> 00:26:36,511
The same thing happened to my father.

574
00:26:38,430 --> 00:26:40,265
But he died. Fortunately you…

575
00:26:41,308 --> 00:26:42,600
You did not.

576
00:26:43,351 --> 00:26:45,395
I don't want that to happen again, okay?

577
00:26:46,438 --> 00:26:48,982
Because I don't want
to lose someone I love.

578
00:26:51,735 --> 00:26:54,738
Do you still love me, even if

579
00:26:55,780 --> 00:26:57,866
I'm upset with you?

580
00:26:59,701 --> 00:27:02,078
Even if you don't like me. [chuckles]

581
00:27:02,162 --> 00:27:03,830
Yes, I love you.

582
00:27:03,913 --> 00:27:06,333
[sentimental music playing]

583
00:27:06,416 --> 00:27:07,876
Let's make up now.

584
00:27:07,959 --> 00:27:11,087
Oh, it's just you who's mad at me, anyway.

585
00:27:11,171 --> 00:27:12,088
It's just you, really.

586
00:27:12,172 --> 00:27:13,465
[scoffs]

587
00:27:18,386 --> 00:27:20,847
[nurse] Sir, I just need
to check the patient.

588
00:27:36,571 --> 00:27:38,573
Don't take this the wrong way, Atoy.

589
00:27:38,656 --> 00:27:39,991
It's not that…

590
00:27:41,034 --> 00:27:43,286
I'm glad that something
happened to Ibyang.

591
00:27:44,454 --> 00:27:46,956
But if we think about it, it's kind of…

592
00:27:47,707 --> 00:27:49,376
a blessing in disguise too.

593
00:27:50,752 --> 00:27:52,045
Because she stopped you.

594
00:27:52,128 --> 00:27:53,963
[pensive music playing]

595
00:27:54,547 --> 00:27:56,841
Think about it.
Had you rushed to confront Red earlier,

596
00:27:58,009 --> 00:27:59,594
you'd have been at a disadvantage.

597
00:28:00,136 --> 00:28:01,721
There are too many of them.

598
00:28:02,931 --> 00:28:04,391
You probably would have been killed there.

599
00:28:05,225 --> 00:28:06,351
You're not allowed to die, right?

600
00:28:08,561 --> 00:28:09,771
He's lucky

601
00:28:11,481 --> 00:28:14,109
because he'll still make it
until tomorrow.

602
00:28:14,192 --> 00:28:16,653
[rousing music playing]

603
00:28:20,281 --> 00:28:21,199
‪[electronic blipping]

604
00:28:30,583 --> 00:28:32,210
[Atoy] <i>You have</i>
<i>lots of other friends, right?</i>

605
00:28:32,293 --> 00:28:33,211
UP NEXT

606
00:28:33,294 --> 00:28:34,587
I want you to stay away from Karla.

607
00:28:34,671 --> 00:28:36,840
I don't have any bad intentions
towards Karla.

608
00:28:36,923 --> 00:28:40,593
Believe me. This will be better for her.

609
00:28:41,594 --> 00:28:43,221
The Sister Norma who suddenly disappeared?

610
00:28:43,304 --> 00:28:46,057
[Mongki] <i>My guy found out</i>
<i>she moved to the province</i>

611
00:28:46,141 --> 00:28:47,142
<i>and then went to Manila.</i>

612
00:28:47,225 --> 00:28:48,017
Have you found her already?

613
00:28:48,101 --> 00:28:49,060
[henchman] Hey!

614
00:28:49,894 --> 00:28:51,312
What are you doing here?!

615
00:28:51,396 --> 00:28:52,689
- [groaning]
- Hey!

616
00:28:58,069 --> 00:28:59,362
[grunting and groaning]

617
00:28:59,446 --> 00:29:01,489
- [thumping]
- [gunfire]

618
00:29:01,573 --> 00:29:02,615
[grunting]

619
00:29:02,699 --> 00:29:04,909
[gunshots]

620
00:29:04,993 --> 00:29:08,538
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

621
00:29:08,621 --> 00:29:09,706
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

622
00:29:09,789 --> 00:29:11,750
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
